  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Suppose $a,b,c\\in\\mathbb Z$. Consider the statement: If $a$ divides $b$ or $c$, then $a$ divides $bc$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove this statement.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$bc=a(kc)$ when $b=ak$, or $bc=a(bk)$ when $c=ak$, with $k\\in\\mathbb Z$. Hence $a$ divides $bc$.",
          "worked": "If $a$ divides $b$, write $b=ak$ for some $k\\in\\mathbb Z$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}bc&=(ak)c\\\\bc&=a(kc).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $kc\\in\\mathbb Z$, $a$ divides $bc$.\n\nIf $a$ divides $c$, write $c=ak$ for some $k\\in\\mathbb Z$. Then $bc=a(bk)$, so again $a$ divides $bc$. Thus the statement holds in either case.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Write down the converse and prove that it is not true.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Converse: If $a$ divides $bc$, then $a$ divides $b$ or $c$.\n\nFalse: $a=6$, $b=4$, $c=3$ gives $bc=12$, but $6$ divides neither $4$ nor $3$.",
          "worked": "Converse: If $a$ divides $bc$, then $a$ divides $b$ or $c$.\n\nTake $a=6$, $b=4$ and $c=3$. Then $bc=12=6\\times2$, so $a$ divides $bc$. However, $6$ divides neither $4$ nor $3$. This counterexample disproves the converse.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
